\title{Nova and Folding Schemes}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Folding two [R1CS](dhsorens-002S) instances into one without proving either, deferring all the
    SNARK work to the end. Also a case study in why this material needs formalising: a soundness bug
    was found in the published scheme.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Relaxed R1CS and committed relaxed R1CS: why the relaxation is needed to make folding
        close.}
        \li{The folding step and its knowledge-soundness argument.}
        \li{Why the recursive circuit is small — the folding verifier, not a SNARK verifier.}
        \li{The bug: what the flaw was, what it permitted, and which part of the argument would have
        caught it under [machine-checked](dhsorens-003Z) scrutiny.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [how Nova got broken](https://blog.zksecurity.xyz/posts/nova-attack/),
    [awesome-folding](https://github.com/lurk-lab/awesome-folding).
}
